# Prototype Stack

## Core Stack

| Decision | Chosen | Alternative |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js (App Router) | Plain React + Vite (simpler, but less AI tooling support) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | CSS Modules or plain CSS |
| Components | Shadcn/ui + TDS4 (when available) | Building custom components from scratch |
| Language | TypeScript (relaxed) | JavaScript (no types at all) |
| Package manager | npm | yarn, pnpm |
| Database | None by default — mock data only | If you need a real backend, ask Cursor to "add a backend" and it will walk you through Supabase setup (see supabase.mdc) |
| Deployment | Vercel | None — run locally only |

---

## Why These Choices

- **Next.js** — AI tools like Cursor and Claude Code default to it, so generated code needs less correction. Deploys to Vercel with zero config.
- **Tailwind** — styles live inline, no separate CSS files to manage. Faster to iterate.
- **Shadcn/ui** — pre-built accessible components that use Tailwind. Swap for TDS4 components as they become available.
- **TypeScript relaxed** — gives some type safety without slowing down prototype speed.
- **No database by default** — mock data is faster and enough for most prototype testing. If a prototype needs real data or persistence, ask Cursor to "add a backend" and it will trigger the Supabase setup flow.

